[WORK]
UID: WORK-EPHEMERAL-ANNOTATION-SEMANTICS
TITLE: Work out annotation that is not meant to last, and whether DEPTH survives it
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
DEPTH is a bad field and the annotation vocabulary around it is underdefined.
Two separate problems, worth drilling into together.

DEPTH names a design-maturity ladder -- sketch, needs-design, needs-spike,
interface-settled, implemented, verified -- and the word says nothing of the
kind. It reads as distance from a root, which is what a person meets it
expecting. DEC-WORK-STATE-FIELD already asks what it means on a WORK node and
is open; this is the wider question of whether the field earns its place at
all, and under what name.

The gap it sits next to: there is no way to annotate a node with something
NOT meant to survive to main. Comments, observed gaps, working notes, a
verdict left for the next session -- none of them are durable claims, and
today the only places to put them are NOTES on a real node or a new node that
outlives its usefulness. The corpus grows and nothing prunes it.

COMMENTARY exists as an element and nothing in the corpus is one; whether it
is the answer here, or whether ephemeral annotation is a different thing
again, is part of the question rather than the answer to it.

Not this session's to carry.
<<<
